    [   0] m "I hate how hard it is to form habits..."
    [   1] m "There's so much stuff where actually doing it isn't hard, but forming the habit seems impossible."
    [   2] m "It just makes you feel so useless, like you can't do anything right."
    [   3] m "I think the new generation suffers from it the most..."
    [   4] m "Probably because we have a totally different set of skills than those who came before us."
    [   5] m "Thanks to the internet, we're really good at sifting through tons of information really quickly..."
    [   6] m "But we're bad at doing things that don't give us instant gratification."
    [   7] m "I think if science, psychology, and education don't catch up in the next ten or twenty years, then we're in trouble."
    [   8] m "But for the time being..."
    [   9] m "If you're not one of the people who can conquer the problem, you might just have to live with feeling awful about yourself."
    [  10] m "Good luck, I guess!"
